{"product_id":"sweetsmoke","title":"Sweetsmoke","description":"\u003cp\u003e\"The year is 1862, and the Civil War is in full flame. Cassius, a slave and carpenter on a tabacco plantation owned by the indomitable Hoke Howard, risks everything - extreme punishment, sale to a cotton plantation, even his life - to learn the truth concerning the murder of a freed black woman, a woman who secretly taught him to read and once saved his life. No one gives a damn about his small, rude, unimportant death in the midst of a brutal and hellish war. No one but Cassius, who braves unimaginable dangers to escape the plantation and avenge her death.\"--Back cover. \u003cbr\u003e\n Dimensions:20 x 233  \u003cbr\u003e\n Author: David Fuller \u003cbr\u003e\n ISBN: 9780349121550 \u003cbr\u003e\n Format: Paperback \u003cbr\u003e\n Pages 320\u003c\/p\u003e","brand":"bookloopbook.com","offers":[{"title":"Default Title","offer_id":43520699400345,"sku":"14RD9780349121550","price":20.0,"currency_code":"AED","in_stock":true}],"thumbnail_url":"\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0580\/5696\/6297\/products\/af9e60648466fb33bd74027441135305.jpg?v=1698145285","url":"https:\/\/bookloopbook.com\/products\/sweetsmoke","provider":"Dubai - Buy Used\/Second-Hand Books - Book Loop Book","version":"1.0","type":"link"}